    "title": "Arianna-Marie Sookram | DTU 2025 Fellow & Gen Z Digital Strategist at Howard University",
    "text": "The Mayor’s Office for Caribbean Community Affairs (MOCCA) hosted its Third Annual Caribbean Cultural Concert at Freedom Plaza, featuring music, parades, food, and activities to celebrate and promote Caribbean culture in Washington, D.C.\nAuthor Archives: Arianna-Marie Sookram\nArianna-Marie Sookram is a DTU 2025 Fellow and a first-generation Afro-Caribbean Communication Studies major with a minor in Economics at Howard University. Maintaining a 3.8 GPA, she has been recognized as a two-time Dean’s List honoree and Founders Scholar. Originally from Trinidad and Tobago, Arianna-Marie’s passion lies at the intersection of media, law, and business. Her work as a Campus Brand Ambassador and Digital Strategist for major brands—including Glow Recipe, NARS, Stanley, Doritos, and Walmart—has enabled her to lead multi-platform campaigns, manage influencer partnerships, and craft content strategies that resonate with Gen Z audiences.",
